; ASSERT ptr=517
; What must be clear on entry is what this routine ADDS into: hashcore's
; two counts and its prefix buffer; A blanket claim over the whole frame
; was wrong and said so the second time HKDF entered here; hashcore
; leaves its digest in H and the last block's schedule in the window  and
; is entitled to  because it clears both itself on the way in;
; ASSERT zero 520:779

; ==== is the key longer than a block ====
; HMAC replaces a key longer than sixty four bytes with its hash; the
; comparison is sixty four borrowing decrements of a copy  which is
; cheaper to write and to read than a general one;
