; ==== the padded key and the length copy are emptied first ====
; Both pads COPY the padded key rather than spend it  because each needs
; it; so it is still full when this routine is entered again  and HKDF
; enters it once to extract and once for every thirty two bytes it
; expands; The second key would be added to the first;
; the padded key
